# Copy this file to .env, then fill in BOTH values below. Never commit .env.
#
# SPLUNK_PASSWORD  The Splunk "admin" password YOU choose. At least 8 characters; use only letters and digits
#                  (characters such as $ # " ' and spaces are mangled by Docker Compose).
#                  Example:  python3 -c "import secrets; print('Ns' + secrets.token_hex(12))"
# SPLUNK_HEC_TOKEN A new GUID.
#                  Example:  python3 -c "import uuid; print(uuid.uuid4())"
#
# IMPORTANT: Splunk stores the admin password the FIRST time it starts with a new data volume. After that the value here must
# always match the password Splunk actually has. If you change the password in Splunk Web, change it here too. If the two
# differ (or the first start was interrupted), Splunk fails with "401 Unauthorized" and the container keeps restarting.
# To start over on a new password: docker compose down -v   (this DELETES the Splunk data volumes), edit .env, docker compose up -d.
SPLUNK_PASSWORD=
SPLUNK_HEC_TOKEN=
